## Codex-Specific Instructions

- Always pass `--no-daemon` when launching Codex in watched Herdr tabs
  (`["codex", "--no-daemon", ...]`) so each tab owns its process.
- Keep `[shell_environment_policy]` `inherit = "all"` (managed via the
  `~/.codex/config.toml/shell-env-policy` merge) so scoped `fnox proxy run`
  CA and proxy variables on the managed allowlist reach shell tools. Keep the
  required variables in a stdio MCP server's own `env_vars` when configuring it.
- Plugin hooks must stay trusted: after plugin installs or upgrades, verify the
  hook-trust registry matches live `hooks/list` hashes (`codex-hook-trust`
  doctor check). Review changed user hook sources and approve them through
  Codex `/hooks`.
- Skills are discovered natively from `~/.agents/skills/`.
